---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.ts';

const updated = '24 September 2026';
---

<Page title="Privacy" description={`What ${site.name} does with your phone number and the other details you give us.`}>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="What happens to your phone number." narrow lede={`In plain English. Last updated ${updated}.`} />

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap--narrow prose">
      {
        site.demo.enabled && (
          <div class="privacy-demo">
            <p>
              <strong>This is a demo site.</strong> {site.name} is not a real gym. If you use the booking form here, your
              details go to {site.demo.author}, who built the site, so he can show gym owners how the funnel works. No gym
              will call you. Demo bookings are deleted within 30 days. To have yours deleted sooner, contact him through{' '}
              <a href={site.demo.authorUrl}>his website</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        )
      }

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you book a {site.offer}, we ask for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name and mobile number,</li>
        <li>the area you live or work in,</li>
        <li>what you want most from training, and when you can usually train.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We also note which page or ad brought you to the site (for example "Facebook ad, trial campaign") and when you
        booked. We never ask for payment details online.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we need it</h2>
      <p>
        To call or WhatsApp you and book your first session, to suggest classes that fit your goal and your day, and to
        know which of our ads are worth paying for.
      </p>

      <h2>Who sees it</h2>
      <p>
        Our front desk and coaches. The booking form is delivered to our email by a form service; it does not use your
        details for anything else. We don't sell your number or share it with anyone who wants to sell you something.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        If you don't join after your {site.offer}, we delete your details after six months. If you become a member, we
        keep them while you are a member and for a year after, then delete them.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and measurement</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics and the Meta Pixel to count visits and bookings, so we can tell which pages and ads help
        people find us. They receive what happened ("someone booked a trial week"), never your name or phone number. You
        can block them with your browser's privacy settings or an ad blocker, and the site will still work.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Message us on WhatsApp or
        ask at the front desk, and we will do it within seven days.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap--narrow">
      <p>
        <a class="link" href="/trial">Back to the {site.offer}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  .privacy-demo {
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1.5px dashed var(--brick);
    background: #fff6f0;
  }
</style>
